Subject: Re: SDK adoption checklist & endpoint cutover timeline

Alex — short answers inline and a tiny sample snippet you can paste.

1) Staging endpoint is identical for both samples; the client just needs the same BASE_URL env var.

2) Yes: client-side exponential backoff (start 200ms, cap 4s) + honor Retry-After for 429. Add a jitter of +-20% to avoid thundering herd.

3) 150 qps peak: we recommend enabling our client-side connection pooling and setting keepalive=true to reduce TLS overhead. Also consider batching small prompts into multi-prompt calls for throughput.

Node sample (pseudo):

const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference-sdk');
const client = new Redwood({ baseUrl: process.env.RW_BASE_URL, apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });

async function safeGenerate(payload) {
  let attempts = 0;
  while (attempts < 5) {
    try {
      return await client.generate(payload, { timeoutMs: 7000 }); // per-call timeout
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.code === 429 && err.headers['retry-after']) {
        await sleep(parseInt(err.headers['retry-after'], 10) * 1000 + jitter());
      } else if (isTransient(err)) {
        await sleep(backoff(attempts));
      } else throw err;
    }
    attempts++;
  }
  throw new Error('max attempts reached');
}

I attached an expanded retry matrix in the runbook; that includes recommended timeout floors for long-chain chat flows. Happy to pair on tuning once Marco runs the sample.

